# FIXTURE — fabricated credentials, not real tokens. Both segments after the
# first are obvious nonsense. Regression pair for the discord-bot-token rule:
# a 24-char first segment (older bot IDs) and a 26-char N-prefixed segment
# (2018-2022 IDs start with digits 4-7 and encode to N…, which the original
# M[TA] pattern silently missed — and a fixed-25-char pattern can never match
# any real token, since unpadded base64 is never 1 mod 4 in length).
DISCORD_TOKEN=MFakeBotIdFakeBotIdFakeB.f4k3id.FakeTimestampFakeSignatureFAKE0
DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN_2019=NFakeBotIdFakeBotIdFakeBo1.f4k3id.FakeTimestampFakeSignatureFAKE1
